  (any edit clears search_highlight; Ctrl+G brings it back)

- [x] Mouse click to land cursor
  (app owns the mouse: click in the editor lands the cursor, click in
  the tree opens the row, wheel moves 3 lines/rows)

- [x] Highlight only ever grabs the editor screen, not the file tree
  (drag is clamped to the editor rect; past the top/bottom edge it
  scrolls one row per event)

- [x] Mouse selection
  (release copies via OSC 52 plus pbcopy / wl-copy / xclip when
  present; Shift+drag still reaches the terminal's native selection)

- [x] Tabs. 
  (tab bar atop the editor pane; Enter/click opens in a new tab or
  switches to the existing one; Ctrl+W / × close; Opt+H/L cycle,
  Opt+1-9 jump; theme keys tab_active / tab_inactive)

- [x] ctrl w closes the window
  (implemented as "close the open file": autosave, back to the launch
  page, tree focused; disk conflict keeps it open)


